            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Illustrated Hungarian Tarokk, also known as Illusztr?lt or Palatinusz Tarokk, is a Hungarian Tarokk variant from the 1920s that adds six extra bonuses to Paskievics Tarokk.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Developed in the late 19th and early 20th centuries as Hungarian players sought to add more tactical variety to the traditional Paskievics-tarokk. It became the 'Illustrated' version because of the numerous 'figures' (bonuses) that decorate the scoring sheet.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
